# RUN: python3 %S/native-owned-global-maps.py --translate ctjs-translate --opt ctjs-opt --work %t

# A published setter takes independently proved primitive actuals while the
# sibling getter retains its zero-argument signature. Saved typed C++ callables
# receive new keys after startup and retain the same Map after owner release.
# Missing, extra, mixed and unproved actuals must preserve every source call.
# Primitive-producing sibling calls retain their typed results and runtime
# order, including two mutating actuals, repeated calls and local aliases.
# Missing/unknown/mixed results and circular evidence remain refusals.
# Method-local per-key set facts prove a later get only for its same live key and
# independently typed payload. Possible same-key writes join payload tags while
# preserving definite presence; repeated writes, saved keys and distinct formal
# actuals retain runtime lookups, result operands and the shared Map lifetime.
# Missing, deleted, cleared and incompatibly joined facts refuse. An exact-key
# reseed restores its own tag without authorizing unsupported payload carriers.
# Distinct definite keys bound the size of their runtime Map; saved size reads
# retain that bound after later growth or deletion of every seeded key. Aliases
# preserve the snapshot. Repeated and possibly equal SSA keys never count twice.
# Removed entries and reads before later seeding cannot inflate the bound;
# equal positive keys/snapshots can alias and must refuse without changing calls.
# Blinded executions distinguish saved/current size and real deletion; fresh/stale
# forged presence, reruns and budget cutoffs stay bounded.
